# Paths Speakeasy generation must never write to or clean up.
#
# scripts/ only holds thin wrappers that delegate to the real implementations
# in ci/ (which is outside the generator's output paths entirely and therefore
# untouchable by construction). Without this file, `speakeasy run` rewrites
# scripts/publish.sh with its naive `uv build && uv publish --token` template
# and silently drops the dual attio/gtm-attio release pipeline.
#
# ci/post_generate_patch.py additionally restores the wrappers after every
# generation in case this ignore file ever stops being honored.
scripts/

# With the target rooted at generated/, Speakeasy also emits project scaffolding
# next to src/. The real pyproject.toml, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and .gitignore
# are hand-maintained at the repo root, so never write them here. The leading
# `/` anchors each entry to generated/ itself: a bare `README.md` also matched
# every generated/docs/sdks/*/README.md and froze the per-method docs.
/pyproject.toml
/README.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/.gitignore

# Speakeasy's compile step runs mypy with cwd=generated/, where the root
# pyproject.toml mypy config is not read; this file stands in for it.
mypy.ini
